#. TRANSLATORS: faq, antwoord met een link naar de privacy-pagina
#: app/faq.py:18
#, python-format
msgid "As little as possible. Your username, your email address for recovery and what you post yourself. Extra profile details only if you fill them in yourself. The details are on the <a href=\"%(url)s\">privacy page</a>."
msgstr "As little as possible. Your username, your email address for recovery and what you post yourself. Extra profile details only if you fill them in yourself. The details are on the <a href=\"%(url)s\">privacy page</a>."

#. TRANSLATORS: faq, vraag 4.3b (the voluntary questions about age, gender,
#. education and country after the first vote)
#: app/faq.py:24
msgid "Why do you ask about my age and education after my first vote?"
msgstr "Why do you ask about my age and education after my first vote?"

#. TRANSLATORS: faq, antwoord 4.3b, met een link naar de privacy-pagina
#: app/faq.py:26
#, python-format
msgid "So that we can show with the result how diverse the group of voters is. It is voluntary and your vote counts either way. We only show totals of groups of at least 10 people, never who voted what. There is more on the <a href=\"%(url)s\">privacy page</a>."
msgstr "So that we can show with the result how diverse the group of voters is. It is voluntary and your vote counts either way. We only show totals of groups of at least 10 people, never who voted what. There is more on the <a href=\"%(url)s\">privacy page</a>."

#. TRANSLATORS: faq, antwoord 3.5. The statuses Reader, Contributor, Voter,
#. Moderator and Senior in lower case; %(voter_min)s, %(moderator_min)s,
#. %(moderator_min_topics)s and %(senior_min)s are numbers.
#: app/faq.py:33
#, python-format
msgid "By contributing quality. Everyone starts as a reader. After your first quality contribution you are a contributor. With %(voter_min)s quality contributions you become a voter, and then you may vote. With more than %(moderator_min)s quality contributions in at least %(moderator_min_topics)s topics you become a moderator. With more than %(senior_min)s you become a senior. That way, what you bring in counts, not just having an account."
msgstr "By contributing quality. Everyone starts as a reader. After your first quality contribution you are a contributor. With %(voter_min)s quality contributions you become a voter, and then you may vote. With more than %(moderator_min)s quality contributions in at least %(moderator_min_topics)s topics you become a moderator. With more than %(senior_min)s you become a senior. That way, what you bring in counts, not just having an account."

#. TRANSLATORS: faq, thema 1
#. TRANSLATORS: faq, vraag 1.1 en antwoord 1.1
#: app/faq.py:44
msgid "What is Global Union?"
msgstr "What is Global Union?"

#: app/faq.py:45
msgid "Global Union is the idea of a partnership of functioning democracies worldwide. It is built on attraction instead of force, following the example of the European Union. It is open to countries that respect the rule of law, human rights, the fight against corruption, sustainability and the international legal order."
msgstr "Global Union is the idea of a partnership of functioning democracies worldwide. It is built on attraction instead of force, following the example of the European Union. It is open to countries that respect the rule of law, human rights, the fight against corruption, sustainability and the international legal order."

#. TRANSLATORS: faq, vraag 1.2 en antwoord 1.2
#: app/faq.py:50
msgid "What is the difference between Global Union and the Global Union Forum?"
msgstr "What is the difference between Global Union and the Global Union Forum?"

#: app/faq.py:51
msgid "Global Union is the idea and the movement. The Global Union Forum is the place where that idea is developed and discussed. Here you think along, bring in facts and vote. Experts and beginners do this side by side."
msgstr "Global Union is the idea and the movement. The Global Union Forum is the place where that idea is developed and discussed. Here you think along, bring in facts and vote. Experts and beginners do this side by side."

#. TRANSLATORS: faq, vraag 1.3 en antwoord 1.3
#: app/faq.py:55
msgid "Who is behind the platform?"
msgstr "Who is behind the platform?"

#: app/faq.py:56
msgid "It is an independent initiative, set up by founder Gerhard Top. With enough momentum, this initiative will be placed in a foundation. The idea is to involve co-initiators first, and then a growing group of participants and experts, to develop it further together."
msgstr "It is an independent initiative, set up by founder Gerhard Top. With enough momentum, this initiative will be placed in a foundation. The idea is to involve co-initiators first, and then a growing group of participants and experts, to develop it further together."

#. TRANSLATORS: faq, vraag 1.4 en antwoord 1.4
#: app/faq.py:60
msgid "Is this linked to a political party or a government?"
msgstr "Is this linked to a political party or a government?"

#: app/faq.py:61
msgid "No. The forum is independent and not linked to a party, a government or a company. It is reformist and it is not tied to a political colour."
msgstr "No. The forum is independent and not linked to a party, a government or a company. It is reformist and it is not tied to a political colour."

#. TRANSLATORS: faq, vraag 1.5 en antwoord 1.5
#: app/faq.py:64
msgid "How can I take part or contribute?"
msgstr "How can I take part or contribute?"

#: app/faq.py:65
msgid "Create an account and read the ground rules. Then you can start: add facts, give your opinion or start an issue yourself. What this becomes is decided by the people who take part."
msgstr "Create an account and read the ground rules. Then you can start: add facts, give your opinion or start an issue yourself. What this becomes is decided by the people who take part."

#. TRANSLATORS: faq, thema 2
#: app/faq.py:69 app/templates/_footer.html:18 app/templates/_header.html:14
msgid "Manifesto"
msgstr "Manifesto"

#. TRANSLATORS: faq, vraag 2.1 en antwoord 2.1
#: app/faq.py:71
msgid "What is in the manifesto?"
msgstr "What is in the manifesto?"

#: app/faq.py:72
msgid "The manifesto from March 2026 is a personal essay by the founder. In it he sets out the idea of a global union of functioning democracies: why it is needed, how it could work and why it is worth trying. See it as the start of the discussion."
msgstr "The manifesto from March 2026 is a personal essay by the founder. In it he sets out the idea of a global union of functioning democracies: why it is needed, how it could work and why it is worth trying. See it as the start of the discussion."

#. TRANSLATORS: faq, vraag 2.2 en antwoord 2.2
#: app/faq.py:76
msgid "What does \"a union of functioning democracies\" mean?"
msgstr "What does \"a union of functioning democracies\" mean?"

#: app/faq.py:77
msgid "A partnership of countries that truly uphold democracy and the rule of law. Countries from all over the world can join. What counts is whether a country meets those values."
msgstr "A partnership of countries that truly uphold democracy and the rule of law. Countries from all over the world can join. What counts is whether a country meets those values."

#. TRANSLATORS: faq, vraag 2.3 en antwoord 2.3
#: app/faq.py:80
msgid "Why the example of the European Union?"
msgstr "Why the example of the European Union?"

#: app/faq.py:81
msgid "The EU shows that countries can work together voluntarily, based on shared rules. They attract each other instead of forcing each other. We want to apply that principle on a world scale."
msgstr "The EU shows that countries can work together voluntarily, based on shared rules. They attract each other instead of forcing each other. We want to apply that principle on a world scale."

#. TRANSLATORS: faq, vraag 2.4 en antwoord 2.4
#: app/faq.py:84
msgid "Which countries could join, and on what basis?"
msgstr "Which countries could join, and on what basis?"

#: app/faq.py:85
msgid "Countries that meet standards such as the rule of law, human rights, the fight against corruption and the international legal order. Membership is based on democratic performance. Not only wealthy Western countries, but also, and especially, model countries from Africa and South America."
msgstr "Countries that meet standards such as the rule of law, human rights, the fight against corruption and the international legal order. Membership is based on democratic performance. Not only wealthy Western countries, but also, and especially, model countries from Africa and South America."

#. TRANSLATORS: faq, vraag 2.5 en antwoord 2.5
#: app/faq.py:90
msgid "Is this not too grand or too idealistic?"
msgstr "Is this not too grand or too idealistic?"

#: app/faq.py:91
msgid "It is a grand idea. Perhaps hard to achieve, but worth it. You start small and build it up together, step by step."
msgstr "It is a grand idea. Perhaps hard to achieve, but worth it. You start small and build it up together, step by step."

#. TRANSLATORS: faq, thema 3
#: app/faq.py:95
msgid "How it works"
msgstr "How it works"

#. TRANSLATORS: faq, vraag 3.1 en antwoord 3.1
#: app/faq.py:97
msgid "How does an issue go, from discussion to vote?"
msgstr "How does an issue go, from discussion to vote?"

#: app/faq.py:98
msgid "Someone starts an issue with a question or problem. In the first phase, facts and discussion, you bring in facts, research and media and discuss it together. Proposals come out of that. After that, the proposer can revise a proposal. Then there is a vote. If the initiator chose so, a summary proposal follows, with a new vote. Finally there is the follow-up phase: what happens with it, such as lobbying, media or implementation."
msgstr "Someone starts an issue with a question or problem. In the first phase, facts and discussion, you bring in facts, research and media and discuss it together. Proposals come out of that. After that, the proposer can revise a proposal. Then there is a vote. If the initiator chose so, a summary proposal follows, with a new vote. Finally there is the follow-up phase: what happens with it, such as lobbying, media or implementation."

#. TRANSLATORS: faq, vraag 3.2 en antwoord 3.2
#: app/faq.py:104
msgid "What are facts, research and media, and how do they count?"
msgstr "What are facts, research and media, and how do they count?"

#: app/faq.py:105
msgid "Facts, research and media are well-founded contributions with a source. Media are news items, podcasts or videos. Each fact has a direction: argues for, argues against or neutral. A fact gets a green quality mark when the AI finds a source, a findable link, where in the source it is, that it is on the topic and that it is new. The mark does not judge how reliable the source is."
msgstr "Facts, research and media are well-founded contributions with a source. Media are news items, podcasts or videos. Each fact has a direction: argues for, argues against or neutral. A fact gets a green quality mark when the AI finds a source, a findable link, where in the source it is, that it is on the topic and that it is new. The mark does not judge how reliable the source is."

#. TRANSLATORS: faq, vraag 3.3 en antwoord 3.3
#: app/faq.py:111
msgid "How do proposals come about, and how is the vote held?"
msgstr "How do proposals come about, and how is the vote held?"

#: app/faq.py:112
msgid "Proposals come out of the discussion. A proposal goes on the voting list as soon as enough people support it. Each proposal is voted on with for, against or abstain. Based on all proposals and the discussion, the initiator can adjust the issue and make a summary proposal. The participants can then vote on that again."
msgstr "Proposals come out of the discussion. A proposal goes on the voting list as soon as enough people support it. Each proposal is voted on with for, against or abstain. Based on all proposals and the discussion, the initiator can adjust the issue and make a summary proposal. The participants can then vote on that again."

#. TRANSLATORS: faq, vraag 3.4 en antwoord 3.4
#: app/faq.py:117
msgid "What is the quality mark?"
msgstr "What is the quality mark?"

#: app/faq.py:118
msgid "A medal that is given automatically to a contribution that moves the discussion forward. That can be a new argument or support with a source. No quality mark is not a punishment. Style and language skills do not count."
msgstr "A medal that is given automatically to a contribution that moves the discussion forward. That can be a new argument or support with a source. No quality mark is not a punishment. Style and language skills do not count."

#. TRANSLATORS: faq, vraag 3.5 en antwoord 3.5
#: app/faq.py:122
msgid "How do I earn the right to vote?"
msgstr "How do I earn the right to vote?"

#. TRANSLATORS: faq, vraag 3.6 en antwoord 3.6
#: app/faq.py:125
msgid "Which ground rules apply, and what happens when they are broken?"
msgstr "Which ground rules apply, and what happens when they are broken?"

#: app/faq.py:126
msgid "There are conduct rules: stay respectful, stay on topic and one account per person. These are enforced. There are also quality guidelines, such as well-founded and concrete. These are rewarded and not enforced. When a rule is clearly broken, a contribution moves to a public background page with an explanation. You can object to that there. Nothing is removed for good. Only pure spam and gross abuse are hidden completely."
msgstr "There are conduct rules: stay respectful, stay on topic and one account per person. These are enforced. There are also quality guidelines, such as well-founded and concrete. These are rewarded and not enforced. When a rule is clearly broken, a contribution moves to a public background page with an explanation. You can object to that there. Nothing is removed for good. Only pure spam and gross abuse are hidden completely."

#. TRANSLATORS: faq, vraag 3.7 en antwoord 3.7
#: app/faq.py:132
msgid "How do you prevent double voting or fake accounts?"
msgstr "How do you prevent double voting or fake accounts?"

#: app/faq.py:133
msgid "It cannot be prevented completely. A new account starts at zero and has to earn the right to vote first, with quality contributions. One account per person is a rule, and moderation steps in when there is abuse. This makes mass fake voting a lot of work for little gain."
msgstr "It cannot be prevented completely. A new account starts at zero and has to earn the right to vote first, with quality contributions. One account per person is a rule, and moderation steps in when there is abuse. This makes mass fake voting a lot of work for little gain."

#. TRANSLATORS: faq, thema 4
#: app/faq.py:138
msgid "Account and privacy"
msgstr "Account and privacy"

#. TRANSLATORS: faq, vraag 4.1 en antwoord 4.1
#: app/faq.py:140
msgid "How do I create an account?"
msgstr "How do I create an account?"

#: app/faq.py:141
msgid "Choose a name and enter an email address. That email address is only for recovery and is never shown. Accept the ground rules and you can start. You do not have to pay and you do not need to show any ID."
msgstr "Choose a name and enter an email address. That email address is only for recovery and is never shown. Accept the ground rules and you can start. You do not have to pay and you do not need to show any ID."

#. TRANSLATORS: faq, vraag 4.2 en antwoord 4.2
#: app/faq.py:145
msgid "Why can I take part under a username?"
msgstr "Why can I take part under a username?"

#: app/faq.py:146
msgid "We want you to be able to join the discussion freely, without having to answer to anyone here. A username makes that possible. In many countries, political participation can bring risks. An identity barrier would shut out exactly the people we want to reach."
msgstr "We want you to be able to join the discussion freely, without having to answer to anyone here. A username makes that possible. In many countries, political participation can bring risks. An identity barrier would shut out exactly the people we want to reach."

#. TRANSLATORS: faq, vraag 4.3 en antwoord 4.3
#: app/faq.py:150
msgid "Which data do you keep, and what for?"
msgstr "Which data do you keep, and what for?"

#. TRANSLATORS: faq, vraag 4.4 en antwoord 4.4
#: app/faq.py:154
msgid "Who can see what I write?"
msgstr "Who can see what I write?"

#: app/faq.py:155
msgid "Your contributions are public and visible under your username. Anyone can read them. Your email address and any private details stay private."
msgstr "Your contributions are public and visible under your username. Anyone can read them. Your email address and any private details stay private."

#. TRANSLATORS: faq, vraag 4.5 en antwoord 4.5
#: app/faq.py:158
msgid "What is the minimum age?"
msgstr "What is the minimum age?"

#: app/faq.py:159
msgid "Sixteen."
msgstr "Sixteen."

#. TRANSLATORS: faq, vraag 4.6 en antwoord 4.6
#: app/faq.py:161
msgid "How do I delete my account or my data?"
msgstr "How do I delete my account or my data?"

#: app/faq.py:162
msgid "You can do that in your account settings or on request. Your personal data, such as your email address and profile, is then erased."
msgstr "You can do that in your account settings or on request. Your personal data, such as your email address and profile, is then erased."

#. TRANSLATORS: faq, vraag 4.7 en antwoord 4.7
#: app/faq.py:165
msgid "What happens to my contributions after I delete my account?"
msgstr "What happens to my contributions after I delete my account?"

#: app/faq.py:166
msgid "Your contributions stay, but are no longer linked to your name. That way, the discussions and votes others took part in keep their coherence. Only the link to you disappears."
msgstr "Your contributions stay, but are no longer linked to your name. That way, the discussions and votes others took part in keep their coherence. Only the link to you disappears."

