#: app/templates/index.html:15
msgid "The world needs a geopolitical power bloc that stands for our security, for our freedom, for the international rule of law, for democracy, human rights and sustainability."
msgstr "The world needs a geopolitical power bloc that stands for our security, for our freedom, for the international rule of law, for democracy, human rights and sustainability."

#: app/templates/index.html:18
msgid "Russia threatens European security, and the US risks becoming a less reliable partner. China backs Russia. The UN Security Council is increasingly paralysed."
msgstr "Russia threatens European security, and the US risks becoming a less reliable partner. China backs Russia. The UN Security Council is increasingly paralysed."

#: app/templates/index.html:21
msgid "Mark Carney, Prime Minister of Canada, called in Davos for cooperation between \"middle powers\": countries that together are large enough to matter and that respect the international rule of law. A first step was taken in October 2026: the EU and Canada formed an alliance for the future, open to like-minded countries."
msgstr "Mark Carney, Prime Minister of Canada, called in Davos for cooperation between \"middle powers\": countries that together are large enough to matter and that respect the international rule of law. A first step was taken in October 2026: the EU and Canada formed an alliance for the future, open to like-minded countries."

#: app/templates/index.html:24
msgid "Global Union Forum wants to seize this momentum and argues for a permanent structure of cooperation, open to all countries that meet criteria for democracy, the rule of law, anti-corruption and human rights. Not as a replacement for the UN, but as a complement. A cooperation alongside the EU, not only with obvious partners such as Canada, the United Kingdom, Japan, South Korea and Australia, but also with countries beyond them that already have a strong democracy, such as Chile, Uruguay, Costa Rica, Cape Verde, Botswana and Ghana."
msgstr "Global Union Forum wants to seize this momentum and argues for a permanent structure of cooperation, open to all countries that meet criteria for democracy, the rule of law, anti-corruption and human rights. Not as a replacement for the UN, but as a complement. A cooperation alongside the EU, not only with obvious partners such as Canada, the United Kingdom, Japan, South Korea and Australia, but also with countries beyond them that already have a strong democracy, such as Chile, Uruguay, Costa Rica, Cape Verde, Botswana and Ghana."

#: app/templates/index.html:27
msgid "With its enlargement into Eastern Europe, the EU showed how strong the pull of a bloc of prosperous democracies is: countries with formerly autocratic regimes carried out reforms in order to join. That pull can be scaled up to the global level, with, in the long term, the prospect of a Global Union of functioning democracies."
msgstr "With its enlargement into Eastern Europe, the EU showed how strong the pull of a bloc of prosperous democracies is: countries with formerly autocratic regimes carried out reforms in order to join. That pull can be scaled up to the global level, with, in the long term, the prospect of a Global Union of functioning democracies."

#: app/templates/index.html:30
msgid "Global Union Forum is an open think tank. We are exploring how this model can work worldwide. A first manifesto has been written. We want to improve it with the knowledge and ideas of everyone who takes part. We will gather all input into a new manifesto. Ultimately with the intention of arriving at a sovereign, resilient and remarkably attractive union of ever more functioning democracies."
msgstr "Global Union Forum is an open think tank. We are exploring how this model can work worldwide. A first manifesto has been written. We want to improve it with the knowledge and ideas of everyone who takes part. We will gather all input into a new manifesto. Ultimately with the intention of arriving at a sovereign, resilient and remarkably attractive union of ever more functioning democracies."

#: app/templates/index.html:34
msgid "We are looking for people who want to think along: experts and laypeople, 17 or 70, convinced or sceptical. Everyone who takes the conversation seriously."
msgstr "We are looking for people who want to think along: experts and laypeople, 17 or 70, convinced or sceptical. Everyone who takes the conversation seriously."

